  // Every portal in the house: the holes, and what is in them.
  //
  // `cna-house.md` §16.1 tabulates L0 and §16.2 the vertical ones; the upper floors and the
  // basement follow the same reading of §13's room schedule. A portal is always an axis-aligned
  // rectangle on an axis-aligned plane (§15.4), and rule 4 checks every one of them lies in
  // BOTH cells' faces -- so these numbers are derived from the cell footprints, never guessed.
  //
  // Windows are `HOUSE-00376`, the garage door and the hatch are `HOUSE-00377`.
  "schema": "cna-house/portals/1",

