    // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // always open — cased openings, stair wells and the open outdoors (`HOUSE-00374`): 47 portals
    // A cased opening is open whether or not anybody has touched anything, and so is a stair
    // well: `IsAlwaysOpen` in `WorldTypes.hpp`, `ALWAYS_OPEN` in `report_graph.py`, and §16.3's
    // second graph -- the one that says the house falls into pieces when every door is shut.
    //
    // Every rectangle here is DERIVED from the two cells' shared wall rather than measured by
    // hand: the run they share, the opening centred in it, and the head above the higher of the
    // two floors. §12.3's cased opening is 1.60 x 2.20 and the wider ones are §16.1's own numbers.
    //
    // The seventeen `EXT_*` to `EXT_*` openings are not in §16.1, which tabulates the house. They
    // are what makes the outdoors one connected place: without them the garden, the orchard and
    // the terrace are each an island, and a pet that walked out of the back door could not reach
    // any of them.
    // `HOUSE-00484`: this is where the basement's door is, because it is where a door can BE. It
    // was a cased opening and the stair's own floor hole carried the leaf; a 1.20 x 2.20 doorway
    // in a wall at the bottom landing takes a normal 0.86 x 2.05 leaf, and shutting it does what
    // shutting the basement door is supposed to do.
